       Products;
   (c) distribute Products you create with the Engine, including Products that
       embed the Engine in compiled form;
   (d) distribute the Engine's source code, modified or unmodified, provided
       every copy retains this License and the notices required by section 3.


3. ATTRIBUTION

   Every Product distributed publicly, whether or not it is commercial, must
   credit the Engine and its original developer. This is a condition of the
   grant, not a request.

   (a) The text "Made with GameWorldshaper" together with "Engine by orgolis"
       must appear in at least one of: a splash or title screen, an in-product
       credits screen, or an "About" dialog reachable from the Product's main
       interface.
   (b) Any documentation, store page or website for the Product that lists the
       technology used must name GameWorldshaper.
   (c) You may not remove, obscure or alter any copyright, attribution or
       license notice in the Engine's source or binaries.

   You may not state or imply that the Licensor endorses, sponsors or is
   affiliated with your Product.


4. ROYALTY ON COMMERCIAL PRODUCTS

   (a) No royalty is owed on any Product whose lifetime Gross Revenue is at or
       below the Threshold. Non-commercial, educational, research, hobby,
       evaluation and internal use are always free of royalty.

   (b) For a Product whose lifetime Gross Revenue exceeds the Threshold, you
       owe the Licensor 5% of the Gross Revenue ABOVE the Threshold. The first
       USD 100,000 per Product is never subject to royalty.

   (c) Royalties are reported and paid quarterly, within 45 days of the end of
       each calendar quarter in which the Threshold was exceeded, using the
       contact address in section 9.

   (d) You must keep records sufficient to determine the amounts owed and
       retain them for three years. The Licensor may request a written
       statement of Gross Revenue for a Product no more than once per year.

   (e) The Licensor may waive or reduce the royalty for any Product in writing.
       If you believe your case warrants a different arrangement, ask before
       shipping rather than after.


